            <ArticleTitle>Facial pain treated by temporomandibular joint arthroscopy and styloidectomy: report of case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>324</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a patient with both Eagle syndrome and temporomandibular joint (TMJ) internal derangement. The patient's pain was relieved by styloidectomy and arthroscopy.</AbstractText>
